3. User Interface Design
   The user interface will be clean, modern, and intuitive, prioritizing ease of use and clear information presentation. A consistent design language will be applied throughout the application to ensure a cohesive user experience.

Dashboard Layout:
Header: Contains the company logo, user avatar with dropdown menu for profile/settings, and global search bar.
Sidebar Navigation: Left-hand navigation panel with clear icons and labels for main modules (e.g., Dashboard, Tasks, Employees, Squads, Reports, Settings). Active module will be highlighted.
Main Content Area: Dynamic area displaying relevant information based on the selected navigation item.
Color Palette: A professional and calming color palette will be used, with clear accent colors for interactive elements and important information.
Typography: A legible and modern font family will be chosen for consistency across all text elements.
Interactive Elements:
Buttons: Clearly labeled and styled buttons for actions (e.g., "Assign Task", "Create Squad", "Submit Feedback").
Forms: Intuitive forms with clear input fields, labels, and validation messages.
Tables: Sortable and filterable tables for data display, with pagination for large datasets.
Graphs & Charts: Visually appealing and interactive graphs to represent performance analytics and task progress.
User Profile Screens: Dedicated screens for employee profiles, allowing users to view and edit personal information, performance metrics, and gamification elements (avatars, badges).
Task Management Views: Kanban boards for squad task management, and detailed task views with fields for description, assignee, status, due date, and feedback.

4. Data Management
   Data management will focus on security, integrity, and efficient access.

Data Storage:
User profiles, company information, roles, tasks, and feedback will primarily be stored in a relational database (e.g., PostgreSQL) to ensure data consistency and support complex queries for hierarchical structures and performance analytics.
Data Models:
Clearly defined data models for each entity (User, Company, Role, Task, Feedback, Squad, etc.) will be established to ensure consistency and facilitate development.
Data Retrieval:
Efficient indexing and query optimization will be implemented to ensure fast data retrieval, especially for dashboards and reports.
Caching mechanisms will be utilized for frequently accessed data to reduce database load and improve response times.
Data Security and Privacy:
All data will be encrypted both in transit (using TLS) and at rest (using database encryption features).
Strict access controls will be applied to the database, ensuring only authorized services and personnel can access sensitive data.
Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) will be implemented to manage and enforce access permissions to sensitive data.
